   "brief": "cough",
   "html": "<div class=\"brief sp\" id=\"cough\" data-entry=\"hub\" data-lens=\"fm\" data-spine=\"2\" data-shelf=\"fm\" data-bp=\"resp\">\n<h4>Chronic Cough</h4>\n<p class=\"sub\">chest film first &middot; postnasal drip, asthma or reflux &middot; angiotensin-converting enzyme (ACE) inhibitor &middot; empiric trials as tests &middot; cancer flags<span class=\"subq\">Is the chest film normal, and which empiric trials have already failed?</span></p>\n<nav class=\"sp-step\" aria-label=\"Decision spine\"><a href=\"#cg-s1\"><b>1</b><span>Presentation</span></a><a href=\"#cg-s2\"><b>2</b><span>Urgent</span></a><a href=\"#cg-dx\"><b>3</b><span>Differential</span></a><a href=\"#cg-s4\"><b>4</b><span>Workup</span></a><a class=\"off\" aria-disabled=\"true\" title=\"Not used in this brief\"><b>5</b><span>Criteria</span></a><a class=\"off\" aria-disabled=\"true\" title=\"Not used in this brief\"><b>6</b><span>Severity</span></a><a class=\"off\" aria-disabled=\"true\" title=\"Not used in this brief\"><b>7</b><span>Treatment</span></a><a class=\"off\" aria-disabled=\"true\" title=\"Not used in this brief\"><b>8</b><span>Follow-up</span></a><a href=\"#cg-bank\" class=\"sp-prac\"><span>Practice</span></a></nav>\n<h5 class=\"tsec sp-h\" id=\"cg-s1\"><b class=\"sp-n\">1</b>Presentation</h5>\n<div class=\"dp\"><span class=\"lbl\">Bottom line</span><ul class=\"bl\"><li><b>Cough over 8 weeks</b> <span class=\"op op-a\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"leads to\"></span> <b>a chest x-ray first</b>, before any empiric trial; check the drug list for an <b>ACE (angiotensin-converting enzyme) inhibitor</b></li><li>Normal film <span class=\"op op-a\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"leads to\"></span> <b>upper airway cough syndrome, asthma or reflux</b></li><li>A finished empiric trial is a test: no response to antihistamines and decongestants effectively <b>excludes postnasal drip</b></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"sp-script sp-s2\"><div class=\"sr\"><span class=\"sk\">What it is</span><div class=\"sv\"><p>Cough lasting more than 8 weeks; under 8 weeks after a cold is postinfectious</p></div></div><div class=\"sr\"><span class=\"sk\">Sort by</span><div class=\"sv\"><p>The film (abnormal: cancer or tuberculosis) <span class=\"op op-p\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"and\"></span> the drug list <span class=\"op op-p\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"and\"></span> which empiric trials have failed</p></div></div><div class=\"sr\"><span class=\"sk\">Hands off</span><div class=\"sv\"><p>Asthma step therapy: Asthma; switching the ACE inhibitor: Hypertension in an Adult; postnasal drip from allergy: Rhinitis; tuberculosis: Tuberculosis</p></div></div></div>\n<h5 class=\"tsec sp-h\" id=\"cg-s2\"><b class=\"sp-n\">2</b>Urgent risks</h5>\n<div class=\"sp-rows\">\n<div class=\"sp-row\"><span class=\"sp-src\">Cancer or tuberculosis</span><b class=\"sp-f\">Weight loss, hemoptysis, smoking or other risk factors</b><div class=\"sp-chips\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"sp-drw\" data-brief=\"tb\">Tuberculosis</button></div><p class=\"sp-commit\"><b>If</b> the film is abnormal or red flags are present, <b>choose</b> <span class=\"mask\">chest CT, then biopsy; sputum for acid-fast bacilli if tuberculosis is possible</span>.</p></div>\n</div>\n<h5 class=\"tsec sp-h\" id=\"cg-dx\"><b class=\"sp-n\">3</b>Differential</h5>\n<div class=\"sp-dx\"><table class=\"dense\"><caption>Cause by clue, most common first</caption><thead><tr><th>Cause</th><th>Clue</th><th>Decides it</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><button type=\"button\" class=\"sp-drw\" data-brief=\"rhinitis\">Upper airway cough syndrome (postnasal drip)</button></td><td><span>Throat clearing, drainage, cobblestoned pharynx</span></td><td><span><span class=\"mask\">Response to an antihistamine-decongestant trial; no response effectively excludes it</span></span></td></tr><tr><td><button type=\"button\" class=\"sp-drw\" data-brief=\"asthma\">Cough-variant asthma</button></td><td><span>Dry cough at night or with cold air or exercise; wheeze often absent</span></td><td><span><span class=\"mask\">Normal spirometry, positive methacholine challenge; cough resolves on an inhaled corticosteroid</span></span></td></tr><tr><td>Gastroesophageal reflux</td><td><span>Worse lying down or after meals; hoarseness; heartburn absent in 40 to 75%</span></td><td><span><span class=\"mask\"><b>Cough resolves over 8 weeks</b> of a proton pump inhibitor</span></span></td></tr><tr><td><button type=\"button\" class=\"sp-drw\" data-brief=\"htn-drugs\">ACE inhibitor cough</button></td><td><span>Dry cough on the drug list; starts days to months after the drug</span></td><td><span><span class=\"mask\"><b>Gone 1 to 4 weeks</b> after stopping it; bradykinin is the cause</span></span></td></tr><tr><td>Postinfectious cough</td><td><span>After a cold</span></td><td><span><span class=\"mask\"><b>Under 8 weeks</b> by definition; observe</span></span></td></tr><tr><td>Lung cancer or tuberculosis (can't miss)</td><td><span>Weight loss, hemoptysis, risk factors</span></td><td><span><span class=\"mask\">Abnormal film; CT, then biopsy</span></span></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h5 class=\"tsec sp-h\" id=\"cg-s4\"><b class=\"sp-n\">4</b>Workup</h5>\n<figure class=\"lcp w5a\"><p class=\"kick\">Diagnostic workup</p><p class=\"w5z\">First step</p><div class=\"w5t first\"><div class=\"w5b\"><div class=\"w5c\">Cough over 8 weeks, no imaging yet</div><span class=\"w5ar\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&rarr;</span><div class=\"w5o\"><span class=\"mask w5om\"><span class=\"w5ol\">Chest x-ray</span></span></div></div><div class=\"w5f\"><div class=\"w5fd f1\"><span class=\"t\" lang=\"en\">Abnormal, or red flags</span><span class=\"ld\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span></div><span class=\"w5an f1\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><div class=\"w5m f1\"><span class=\"mask\">Chest CT, then biopsy</span></div><div class=\"w5fd fl\"><span class=\"t\" lang=\"en\">Normal</span><span class=\"ld\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span></div><span class=\"w5an fl\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><div class=\"w5m fl\"><span class=\"mask\">Postnasal drip, asthma or reflux</span></div></div></div><p class=\"w5z\">Targeted tests</p><div class=\"w5t\"><div class=\"w5b\"><div class=\"w5c\">On an ACE inhibitor</div><span class=\"w5ar\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&rarr;</span><div class=\"w5o\"><span class=\"mask w5om\"><span class=\"w5ol\">Stop the drug</span></span></div></div><div class=\"w5f\"><div class=\"w5fd f1 fl\"><span class=\"t\" lang=\"en\">Cough gone in 1 to 4 weeks</span><span class=\"ld\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span></div><span class=\"w5an f1 fl\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><div class=\"w5m f1 fl\"><span class=\"mask\">ACE inhibitor cough; switch to an ARB (angiotensin receptor blocker)</span></div></div><div class=\"w5b\"><div class=\"w5c\">Throat clearing, drainage</div><span class=\"w5ar\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&rarr;</span><div class=\"w5o\"><span class=\"mask w5om\"><span class=\"w5ol\">First-generation antihistamine with a decongestant</span></span></div></div><div class=\"w5f\"><div class=\"w5fd f1\"><span class=\"t\" lang=\"en\">Response</span><span class=\"ld\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span></div><span class=\"w5an f1\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><div class=\"w5m f1\"><span class=\"mask\">Upper airway cough syndrome</span></div><div class=\"w5fd fl\"><span class=\"t\" lang=\"en\">No response</span><span class=\"ld\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span></div><span class=\"w5an fl\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><div class=\"w5m fl\"><span class=\"mask\">Effectively excluded</span></div></div><div class=\"w5b\"><div class=\"w5c\">Night cough, cold air or exercise</div><span class=\"w5ar\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&rarr;</span><div class=\"w5o\"><span class=\"mask w5om\"><span class=\"w5ol\">Spirometry, then methacholine challenge if normal</span></span></div></div><div class=\"w5f\"><div class=\"w5fd f1\"><span class=\"t\" lang=\"en\">Positive challenge</span><span class=\"ld\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span></div><span class=\"w5an f1\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><div class=\"w5m f1\"><span class=\"mask\">Cough-variant asthma</span></div><div class=\"w5fd fl\"><span class=\"t\" lang=\"en\">Negative challenge</span><span class=\"ld\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span></div><span class=\"w5an fl\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><div class=\"w5m fl\"><span class=\"mask\">Asthma ruled out</span></div></div></div><p class=\"w5z\">Next step</p><div class=\"w5t\"><div class=\"w5b\"><div class=\"w5c\">Antihistamine and inhaled steroid trials failed</div><span class=\"w5ar\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&rarr;</span><div class=\"w5o\"><span class=\"mask w5om\"><span class=\"w5ol\">Proton pump inhibitor for 8 weeks</span></span></div></div><div class=\"w5f\"><div class=\"w5fd f1\"><span class=\"t\" lang=\"en\">Cough resolves</span><span class=\"ld\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span></div><span class=\"w5an f1\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><div class=\"w5m f1\"><span class=\"mask\">Reflux</span></div><div class=\"w5fd fl\"><span class=\"t\" lang=\"en\">Refractory</span><span class=\"ld\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span></div><span class=\"w5an fl\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><div class=\"w5m fl\"><span class=\"mask\">pH monitoring; if all three trials fail, refer</span></div></div></div></figure>\n<div class=\"sp-dx\"><table class=\"dense\"><caption>Clues that change the answer</caption><thead><tr><th>Clue</th><th>Points to</th><th>Next move</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Night cough already on a proton pump inhibitor, no postnasal drip</td><td><span><span class=\"mask\">Asthma, not reflux</span></span></td><td><span><span class=\"mask\">Pulmonary function tests for bronchodilator response<div class=\"sp-chips\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"sp-drw\" data-brief=\"asthma\">Asthma</button></div></span></span></td></tr><tr><td>Cough 5 weeks after a cold, normal film</td><td><span><span class=\"mask\">Postinfectious cough</span></span></td><td><span><span class=\"mask\">Observe; work up if it passes 8 weeks</span></span></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<div class=\"sp-pause\"><b class=\"pp-t\">Pause point</b>\n<div class=\"pp-b\">\n<span class=\"sl\">Chronic cough</span>\n<span class=\"si pp-off\">Offered: <em>an empiric trial before imaging</em></span>\n<span class=\"si\"><span class=\"mask\">Every chronic cough</span></span>\n<span class=\"pp-a\">&rarr; <span class=\"mask\">The chest film first</span></span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"pp-b\">\n<span class=\"sl\">Cough that &ldquo;did not respond to&rdquo; a drug</span>\n<span class=\"si pp-off\">Offered as <em>the cause that drug treats</em></span>\n<span class=\"si\"><span class=\"mask\">The stem has already excluded it</span></span>\n<span class=\"pp-a\">&rarr; <span class=\"mask\">Not that cause</span></span>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n<h5 class=\"authored-hdr\" id=\"cg-bank\">Practice</h5>\n<ol class=\"bank authored\">\n<li data-type=\"dx\" data-d1=\"Cough-variant asthma\" data-d2=\"Gastroesophageal reflux\" data-item-id=\"q_ff3483ea03425d9bb7f9\" data-item-version=\"1\" data-item-status=\"ready\" data-key-id=\"o_f7916c41e08452b1bbdd\" data-d1-id=\"o_7e0630e665b553338d4a\" data-d2-id=\"o_b13df36e50285121833c\">45 yo F, 3 months of cough, normal chest X-ray, post-nasal drip and throat clearing → <b>Upper airway cough syndrome</b> → first-generation antihistamine trial</li>\n<li data-type=\"dx\" data-d1=\"Upper airway cough syndrome\" data-d2=\"Postinfectious cough\" data-item-id=\"q_29f87d86f53f5988bebb\" data-item-version=\"1\" data-item-status=\"ready\" data-key-id=\"o_528e298f69bd55aa80d8\" data-d1-id=\"o_bbb1cfccf3b3568ebffc\" data-d2-id=\"o_9baa513c2e4b53868ad3\">45 yo F on lisinopril with 3 months of dry cough → <b>ACE-inhibitor cough</b> → stop the drug</li>\n<li data-type=\"dx\" data-d1=\"Gastroesophageal reflux\" data-d2=\"Postinfectious cough\" data-item-id=\"q_3a156da22bb352deaf0c\" data-item-version=\"1\" data-item-status=\"ready\" data-key-id=\"o_4dbefe2d69dc54569e39\" data-d1-id=\"o_5da78e1d47d05e3db2a7\" data-d2-id=\"o_9ee71565319c57599ebb\">45 yo F whose cough is worse at night and with cold air, spirometry normal → <b>Cough-variant asthma</b> → methacholine challenge</li>\n<li data-type=\"dx\" data-d1=\"Upper airway cough syndrome\" data-d2=\"Cough-variant asthma\" data-item-id=\"q_cf1efb7106535b888d65\" data-item-version=\"1\" data-item-status=\"ready\" data-key-id=\"o_e5f501edfe915184a427\" data-d1-id=\"o_a2d2acfd897650589509\" data-d2-id=\"o_8cff59deeb9c511bb7be\">45 yo F with cough and heartburn after failed antihistamine and inhaled steroid trials → <b>Gastroesophageal reflux</b> → proton pump inhibitor trial</li>\n<li data-type=\"dx\" data-d1=\"Postinfectious cough\" data-d2=\"Upper airway cough syndrome\" data-item-id=\"q_2eb3e4e655e555deadec\" data-item-version=\"1\" data-item-status=\"ready\" data-key-id=\"o_1dd8478bba005d5d95d0\" data-d1-id=\"o_76306a315e3d539591bb\" data-d2-id=\"o_ab32f395038b54c4a1d5\">45 yo F, smoker, cough with hemoptysis and 6 kg weight loss → <b>Malignancy</b> → chest CT</li>\n<li data-type=\"dx\" data-d1=\"Pertussis\" data-d2=\"Nonasthmatic eosinophilic bronchitis\" data-item-id=\"q_36e5ff7ec0c857589e46\" data-item-version=\"1\" data-item-status=\"ready\" data-key-id=\"o_ae9badfde21a5cc8ba2a\" data-d1-id=\"o_fd207a07305f5528aa54\" data-d2-id=\"o_10e4469fcb795919b92b\">45 yo F with cough for 5 weeks after a viral illness, normal chest X-ray → <b>Postinfectious cough</b> → observation</li>\n<li data-type=\"next\" data-src=\"authored\" data-d1=\"Empiric proton pump inhibitor trial\" data-d2=\"Spirometry\" data-item-id=\"q_fcbe19b31dfe0add9435\" data-item-version=\"1\" data-item-status=\"ready\" data-key-id=\"o_e474da947da694f3b8b8\" data-d1-id=\"o_a009f73b4afb2f742fae\" data-d2-id=\"o_ad0c123052318fc6171b\">55 yo M with 10 weeks of cough and no imaging yet &rarr; <b>Chest X-ray</b> &rarr; first in all chronic cough, before any empiric trial</li>\n<li data-type=\"next\" data-src=\"authored\" data-d1=\"Switch to a different ACE inhibitor\" data-d2=\"First-generation antihistamine trial\" data-item-id=\"q_7f9a5d5aad56f5a9ffab\" data-item-version=\"1\" data-item-status=\"ready\" data-key-id=\"o_0c0558fcfcae088acb79\" data-d1-id=\"o_f4cce1ba418ea3d57c5c\" data-d2-id=\"o_92b95827a52ca448432b\">45 yo F on lisinopril with 3 months of dry cough and a normal chest X-ray &rarr; <b>Stop lisinopril</b> &rarr; ACE-inhibitor cough resolves in 1 to 4 weeks</li>\n<li data-type=\"test\" data-src=\"authored\" data-d1=\"24-hour esophageal pH monitoring\" data-d2=\"Chest CT\" data-item-id=\"q_7ef3d8d2d2cbfe7e15c8\" data-item-version=\"2\" data-item-status=\"ready\" data-key-id=\"o_8c02645ee485dcce37e4\" data-d1-id=\"o_eee22821b8e96d3aa859\" data-d2-id=\"o_88c1690ea6d1e3e5c83d\" data-lead-in=\"Which of the following is the most appropriate diagnostic study to obtain at this time?\">30 yo M with chronic cough at night and with exercise and cold air; normal exam and normal spirometry &rarr; <b>Methacholine challenge</b> &rarr; normal spirometry does not exclude cough-variant asthma</li>\n<li data-type=\"next\" data-src=\"authored\" data-d1=\"Methacholine challenge\" data-d2=\"High-resolution chest CT\" data-item-id=\"q_8e8196d602e352b8c519\" data-item-version=\"1\" data-item-status=\"ready\" data-key-id=\"o_40170b6d05c20057e2cf\" data-d1-id=\"o_e7fed71b4551dcecef71\" data-d2-id=\"o_751fc431d74efbfbbc89\">45 yo F with 3 months of dry cough, normal chest X-ray and no heartburn, after failed antihistamine-decongestant and inhaled corticosteroid trials &rarr; <b>Proton pump inhibitor for 8 weeks</b> &rarr; GERD cough is often silent; the failed trials have eliminated the other two</li>\n</ol>\n<div class=\"rule\"><span class=\"lbl\">Transferable rule</span> When a stem says \"did not respond to X,\" it is not giving history; it <b>eliminates the cause X treats</b>. Read treatment failures as eliminations. A dry cough with a normal film, after failed antihistamine-decongestant and inhaled corticosteroid trials, is <b>GERD</b> (gastroesophageal reflux disease) until proven otherwise.</div>\n</div>",
